---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const title = 'About DroidDiagnostics';
const description = 'DroidDiagnostics is a privacy-first Android/AOSP diagnostic workbench that parses supported bugreport evidence locally in the browser.';
---
<BaseLayout {title} {description}>
  <section class="content-page">
    <div class="shell content-shell">
      <header class="content-header">
        <span class="kicker">About</span>
        <h1>Diagnostics should start with evidence.</h1>
        <p>DroidDiagnostics turns large Android diagnostic archives into a smaller, inspectable set of findings while keeping the source archive in the browser.</p>
      </header>
      <section class="card prose-card">
        <h2>Current scope</h2>
        <p>The v0.2 engine inventories modern bugreport archives and triages reboot, ANR, Java/native crash, kernel, Binder, memory, storage, biometric/UDFPS, display, thermal, battery, network, SELinux, and boot evidence. It keeps matching source excerpts visible because a signature is evidence, not automatic proof of root cause.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="card prose-card">
        <h2>Deterministic by design</h2>
        <p>The core parser does not ask an LLM to interpret private diagnostics. Subsystem analyzers use explicit signatures, source context, severity rules, evidence strength, and correlation. Optional explanation layers can be added later without making them the source of truth.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="card prose-card">
        <h2>Designed to become a workbench</h2>
        <p>The next stages are structured ANR/tombstone/BatteryStats parsers, typed dumpstate service models, real-device regression fixtures, A/B comparison, and richer incident timelines. The existing finding model and source inventory are designed so those additions do not require replacing the core pipeline.</p>
      </section>
      <div class="article-actions"><a class="button button-primary" href="/analyze">Open analyzer</a><a class="button" href="/references">Technical references</a></div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
